<article class="env-lemma" id="02R9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02R9">Lemma <span data-tag="02R9">42.13.2</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$, $Y$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism. Assume $\{ Z_ i\} _{i \in I}$ is a locally finite collection of closed subsets of $Y$. Then $\{ f^{-1}(Z_ i)\} _{i \in I}$ is a locally finite collection of closed subsets of $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $U \subset X$ be a quasi-compact open subset. Since the image $f(U) \subset Y$ is a quasi-compact subset there exists a quasi-compact open $V \subset Y$ such that $f(U) \subset V$. Note that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \{ i \in I \mid f^{-1}(Z_ i) \cap U \not= \emptyset \}  \subset \{ i \in I \mid Z_ i \cap V \not= \emptyset \} .  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Since the right hand side is finite by assumption we win. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>